  },
  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 17 May 1961 and counted on Thursday 18 May: eighteen candidates for the three aldermanships and twelve councillorships. The new council was twelve Unionists and three Independents, against thirteen and two before. Labels as printed: U Unionist, I Independent. Turnout not printed. Mrs Winifred A. Monroe (\"Mrs. F. A. Monroe\"), widow of the first Mayor, topped the poll; she and Mrs M. A. Bell were the first women on the council."
}
